  "query_preview": "..\n\n - Meteorological Overview:\n\nBroad upper level troughing continues across the western US, with a \nreinforcing lobe of vorticity/compact upper low diving \nsouth/southeastward through AB and SK toward NE MT through Saturday \nmorning. As the aforementioned upper system approaches this \nafternoon and evening, light to at times moderate snow begins to \nspread over much of the region. Ahead of the area of light to \nmoderate widespread snow, there looks to be marginal, yet sufficient \nlow-level instability to result in a few snow showers, mainly across \nCentral and SW MT. The more widespread snow that develops through \nthe afternoon and evening largely looks to be predominately light \n(snowfall rates of around 1/4\" per hour); however, periods of \nmoderate snow (snowfall rates between 1/2\" to 3/4\" per hour) are \npossible in northerly upslope favored areas. Given colder \ntemperatures in place now, this lighter snow will have better \nsuccess accumulating on roadways. This snow largely diminishes into \nSaturday morning, with areas in northwesterly favored areas seeing \ncontinued light snow through the afternoon Saturday. \n\nTransient ridging briefly builds in Sunday ahead of a much lower \nconfidence forecast heading into next week. Several upper level \ndisturbances off the west coast will be in place to open next week. \nWhether they move east across the Pacific NW or shift southward \nbefore moving east toward the Northern Rockies Monday remains to be \nseen. After the uncertainty to open the week, around 80% of cluster \nguidance members favor some form of at least weak upper level \nridging and associated warmer than average temperatures mid-week \ntoward Thanksgiving. - AM/Moldan\n\n - Forecast Confidence & Scenarios:\n\nImpactful Snow through Saturday Morning...\n\nConfidence has increased that impactful snow will occur from the \nafternoon hours today through Saturday morning across portions of \nNorth Central through Southwest Montana; most notably in \nnortherly upslope favored locations such as the Elkhorn and \nBoulder Mountains, Little Belt and Highwood Mountains, Upper \nBlackfoot and MacDonald Pass, Southern Rocky Mountain Front, East \nGlacier Park Region, Gates of the Mountains, Cascade County below \n5000ft, Northern High Plains, and Southern High Plains, Big Belt, \nBridger and Castle Mountains, Gallatin and Madison County \nMountains and Centennial Mountains, Gallatin Valley, and the \nMadison River Valley. For this reason a Winter Weather Advisory \nhas been issued for the aforementioned locations through the late\nmorning hours on Saturday.\n\nThe table below lists the snowfall amounts for the \u201clow end\u201d (10th \nPercentile), \u201cmost likely\u201d (50th Percentile), and \u201chigh end\u201d (90th \nPercentile) scenarios within the NBM5.2 for select locations across \nNorth Central, Central and Southwest Montana from Friday morning \nthrough Sunday morning.\n\nThe low end scenario has a 90% chance that amounts will exceed the \nlisted value or a 10% chance that amounts will be lower than what is \nlisted while the high end scenario has a 90% chance that amounts \nwill be lower than what is listed or a 10% chance that amounts will \nbe higher than what is listed. The greater the spread between the \nlow end and the high end scenario the greater the uncertainty is \nwith regards to snowfall amounts, with a lower spread between low \nend and high end supporting a lower degree of uncertainty (higher \nconfidence).\n\n                         Snow Scenarios thru Saturday AM\nLOCATION                 10 Pct  |   50 Pct  |   90 Pct\nMarias Pass               1.3\"   |    2.9\"   |    5.0\"\nBrowning                  0.0\"   |    0.2\"   |    2.2\"\nCut Bank                  0.0\"   |    0.0\"   |    1.4\"\nHavre                     0.0\"   |    0.0\"   |    1.0\"\nRogers Pass               1.6\"   |    3.2\"   |    4.6\"\nGreat Falls               0.2\"   |    1.1\"   |    2.9\"\nLewistown                 0.5\"   |    1.0\"   |    2.2\"\nMacDonald Pass            2.8\"   |    4.4\"   |    6.0\"\nHelena                    0.0\"   |    0.3\"   |    1.5\"\nKings Hill Pass           0.9\"   |    1.5\"   |    2.2\"\nBozeman                   0.1\"   |    1.9\"   |    4.2\"\nBozeman Pass              2.3\"   |    5.4\"   |    6.0\"\nDillon                    0.0\"   |    0.0\"   |    0.0\"\nEnnis                     0.0\"   |    0.1\"   |    1.5\"\nWest Yellowstone          0.0\"   |    0.0\"   |    0.8\"\n\n- Moldan",
